    706	| Character-twisted Liouville sums L_chi(x) for chi mod q in {3,5,7,11,13} (FOCUS-2 q>=3 / Chain B) | FAIL | I | Generalizes the S55 q=2 closure to all 34 non-trivial Dirichlet characters across q in {3,5,7,11,13}. ALGEBRAIC FREE IDENTITY: L_chi(x) = sum_{r in (Z/q)*} chi(r)*S_r(x) with S_r(x) = sum_{n<=x, n=r mod q} lambda(n); since each lambda(n) in {-1,+1} ≡ 1 (mod 2), S_r(x) ≡ count_r(x) (mod 2 in Z), hence L_chi(x) ≡ sum_r chi(r)*count_r(x) (mod 2 Z[zeta_d]) where d = ord(chi). Right-hand side computable in O(polylog) via floor counts, no prime info. Verified by EXACT integer arithmetic in Z[zeta_d] (cyclotomic-polynomial reduction; rank-deficient FP-projection appears to fail for d in {5,10,12} but exact check passes 2000/2000 sampled x for ALL 34 chars). Next-bit pseudorandomness: A_chi(x) mod 2 = #{n<=x: lambda(n)*Re(chi(n))=+1} mod 2 has LFSR/N in [0.4995, 0.5002] (full pseudorandom rank), block-entropy up to 7.97/8, FFT z up to 8.5 (within 1.5sigma of order-statistic baseline ~4.8), AC values up to 0.6 are pure coset-density bias 1/phi(d). MAX MI(A_chi mod 2 ; pi(x;q,a) mod 2) = 9.55e-6 bits across all q, all chi, all a in (Z/q)* — at noise floor for N=1e6 samples. Closes the natural extension of S55 to q>=3; the character-twisted route to chain B's missing primitive collapses by the same dual mechanism (free identity + pseudorandom next bit). Adds measures #27..#31 to novel/pseudorandomness_of_pi.md. See experiments/sieve/pi_mod_q_fixed/character_twisted_liouville.py | 56 |
