    6	## Summary
    7	
    8	pi(x) mod 2 is indistinguishable from a random Boolean function under every
    9	structural complexity measure tested in this project (31). This is the
    10	project's strongest collective finding.
    11	
    12	The 2 measures added in S55 (A(x) mod 2, C_3(x) mod 2) probe the COMPONENTS of
    13	the Liouville-identity decomposition pi(x) = (x - L(x))/2 - C_3(x) (E2.2). They
    14	strengthen the picture: even after splitting pi(x) mod 2 = A(x) mod 2 XOR
    15	C_3(x) mod 2, EACH of the two halves is independently pseudorandom and the
    16	two are mutually independent (I(A; C_3) ≈ 2 × 10⁻⁵ bits).  In particular
    17	A(x) mod 2 (equivalently L(x) mod 4 modulo the trivial L mod 2 = x mod 2)
    18	is *more* pseudorandom than pi(x) mod 2 itself — its only nontrivial
    19	auto-structure (sparse density bias) is removed because Omega(n) is odd for
    20	exactly half of n.
